    title: "US judge rules in favour of foreign students and journalists after Trump limits visas",
    summary: "US judge rules in favour of foreign students and journalists after Trump limits visas A US federal judge has thrown out the Trump administration's attempt to limit visas for international students and members of the foreign press after university and media unions filed a lawsuit against the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) in August. Massachusetts District Judge Dennis Saylor said on Monday that the government has been unable to prove there has been widespread visa fraud or national security concerns with this particular visa programme. DHS's move to impose restrictions \"is arbitrary and capricious\", Saylor said in his decision. \"The Final Rule, entitled Establishing a Fixed Time Period of Admission and an Extension of Stay Procedure for Nonimmigrant Academic Students, Exchange Visitors, and Representatives of Foreign Information Media... is hereby VACATED,\" he wrote. Saylor added that DHS is \"seeking to prevent or discourage the very activity - providing educational opportunities for foreign students in the United States - that Congress sought to permit and encourage\". The ruling preserves the \"duration of status\" or \"D/S\" stamp that international students receive on their visas and, by extension, on the visas foreign journalists receive as well. It means they are legally permitted to stay in the country as long as they remain in the status they obtained, either as active students or working journalists, whether it's mere months or several years. ts after Trump limits visas US Secretary of State Marco Rubio takes questions from journalists in the Department of State briefing room during his end-of-year press conference, on 19 December 2025 (Mandel Ngan/AFP)",
